OpenGL compatibility dependencies

gl4es is vendored from https://github.com/ptitSeb/gl4es at commit
a444cc94b17c672c66c3e6ce07428dc603034db1. Its source and headers provide
desktop fixed-function OpenGL over the system OpenGL ES 2 driver.
The upstream source list is used for the static iOS build. The unused legacy
GLU mangling header is omitted; the separate Mesa GLU subset supplies GLU.
The original MIT license is in gl4es/LICENSE; individual files retain their
notices.
The Apple build replaces two unsupported compiler aliases in directstate.c
with forwarding functions.
glstate.c removes a duplicate fixed-function emulator allocation during
context creation and releases the emulator state and ARB matrix pointer
array and immediate-mode index buffer when the context is destroyed.
getter.c handles the local-viewer
and separate-specular lighting queries from the emulator state instead
of forwarding desktop-only enums to OpenGL ES.

GLU contains the quadric and projection utilities from Mesa GLU 9.0.3,
https://archive.mesa3d.org/glu/glu-9.0.3.tar.xz. Tessellation, NURBS and
mipmap utilities are omitted. The files retain the SGI Free Software
License B version 2.0 and original copyright notices.

These components are built from source by Scripts/build-gl-compat.sh.
Native OpenGLES headers remain separate from the gl4es compatibility
headers so the wrapper can resolve the real framework entry points.
Sources/MBCIOSGLBridge.c isolates gl4es' internal context-state API for
independent EAGL contexts, releases its program and shader maps at teardown,
disables the color-renderbuffer replacement workaround so EAGL presents
the actual drawing attachment, and synchronizes tracked renderbuffer dimensions after native drawable
and multisample storage allocation. All wrapper calls run on the main
thread while their corresponding EAGL context is current.
The bridge checks generated program link status before presenting a frame;
the renderer also rejects failed texture uploads during preparation.
